      "tag": "DETAILS",
      "text": "What is the difference between SCIA Concept, Professional, and Ultimate?SCIA Concept focuses on core structural modeling and analysis for everyday engineering projects. SCIA Professional adds advanced engineering workflows, multi-material design, and expanded analysis capabilities. SCIA Ultimate provides the most comprehensive analysis tools for complex structures and advanced structural engineering challenges."
    },
    {
      "tag": "DETAILS",
      "text": "Does SCIA support BIM workflows?Yes. SCIA supports Open BIM workflows and integrates with leading design and detailing platforms such as Allplan, SDS2, Revit, and Tekla. Engineers can exchange models using IFC and SAF formats for efficient collaboration across disciplines."
    },
    {
      "tag": "DETAILS",
      "text": "Which industries use SCIA?SCIA is widely used by structural engineering firms, infrastructure designers, industrial engineering teams, and multidisciplinary AEC practices working on buildings, bridges, industrial facilities, and complex structural projects."
    },
    {
      "tag": "DETAILS",
      "text": "Can I upgrade between SCIA editions later?Yes. SCIA editions are designed to scale with your engineering needs. Teams can upgrade to higher editions as projects become more complex or require advanced structural analysis capabilities."
